{"zh":[{"start":0.33,"end":4.56,"text":"在格陵兰西北部一个偏远的地方，"},{"start":4.56,"end":8.75,"text":"一支国际科学家团队"},{"start":8.75,"end":12.99,"text":"有了惊人的发现，它埋在一公里厚的"},{"start":12.99,"end":17.18,"text":"冰下面。那是一个撞击坑……"},{"start":17.18,"end":21.4,"text":"深 300 米……宽 31 公里……"},{"start":21.4,"end":25.69,"text":"……比华盛顿特区大得多，"},{"start":25.69,"end":29.89,"text":"甚至比巴黎还大，而且它大概"},{"start":29.89,"end":34.15,"text":"是地球上最年轻的大型撞击坑之一。"},{"start":34.15,"end":38.48,"text":"格陵兰冰盖不断扩张，把陨石坑盖住了，让人看不见它，"},{"start":38.48,"end":42.7,"text":"遮住了它，时间就算没有几十万年，也有几千年。"},{"start":42.7,"end":46.91,"text":"即便如此，科学家说它其实一直就藏在眼皮底下。"},{"start":46.91,"end":51.18,"text":"那最后是什么暴露了它的存在？"},{"start":51.18,"end":55.42,"text":"一切都从一块石头……一张地图……"},{"start":55.42,"end":59.61,"text":"还有哥本哈根自然历史博物馆科学家的一个联想开始。"},{"start":59.61,"end":63.92,"text":"那里的科学家每天都会经过一块巨大的"},{"start":63.92,"end":68.12,"text":"铁陨石，是几十年前在格陵兰发现的。"},{"start":68.12,"end":72.33,"text":"有一天，他们拿到一张冰盖下基岩地形的新地图，"},{"start":72.33,"end":76.55,"text":"主要根据穿冰雷达的数据绘制，这些数据是"},{"start":76.55,"end":80.75,"text":"二十年来 NASA 的 P-3 飞机上采集的。"},{"start":80.75,"end":84.95,"text":"这张地图一直在细化，但仍有些地方有待"},{"start":84.95,"end":89.18,"text":"解读，包括冰盖边缘那段明显的半圆形"},{"start":89.18,"end":93.36,"text":"边缘，由海华沙冰川排水。"},{"start":93.36,"end":97.55,"text":"在那里，数据显示基岩上有一个圆形凹陷，"},{"start":97.55,"end":101.77,"text":"就在那块院子里的陨石当年被发现的地方附近。"},{"start":101.77,"end":105.99,"text":"2016 年 5 月，团队派出德国的科研飞机"},{"start":105.99,"end":110.2,"text":"「极地 6 号」，带着一台强大的新型"},{"start":110.2,"end":114.49,"text":"穿冰雷达飞越海华沙冰川。"},{"start":114.49,"end":118.75,"text":"雷达波能穿透冰层，测出冰的厚度"},{"start":118.75,"end":123.08,"text":"和内部结构。研究这次航测的数据，"},{"start":123.08,"end":127.34,"text":"科学家确认了海华沙冰川下面有明显的碗状"},{"start":127.34,"end":131.59,"text":"和中央峰。他们还发现，这个坑里最古老的冰"},{"start":131.59,"end":135.82,"text":"按格陵兰的标准其实相当年轻，"},{"start":135.82,"end":139.93,"text":"而且在末次冰期快结束时，"},{"start":139.93,"end":144.23,"text":"冰的流动受到过一次巨大的扰动。"},{"start":144.23,"end":148.47,"text":"随后团队徒步去了那里，在冰川流出的河"},{"start":148.47,"end":152.69,"text":"所沉积的泥沙里，发现了石英矿物颗粒，带有"},{"start":152.69,"end":156.95,"text":"在巨大撞击中受过物理冲击的痕迹。"},{"start":156.95,"end":161.13,"text":"模型表明，那颗小行星宽度超过一公里。"},{"start":161.13,"end":165.32,"text":"海华沙陨石坑是已知 25 个最大的"},{"start":165.32,"end":169.95,"text":"地球撞击坑之一，也是第一个在"},{"start":169.95,"end":174.26,"text":"我们星球任何冰盖下发现的。关键是，海华沙撞击"},{"start":174.26,"end":178.55,"text":"坑仍然看得出是撞击坑，尽管它被冰盖着，"},{"start":178.55,"end":182.75,"text":"而且似乎在快速侵蚀。数据总体"},{"start":182.75,"end":187.03,"text":"表明它相当年轻——从地质学上说。"},{"start":187.03,"end":191.32,"text":"但我们不知道小行星究竟是什么时候冲向"},{"start":191.32,"end":195.55,"text":"地球，穿过大气层，撞进"},{"start":195.55,"end":199.84,"text":"格陵兰西北部的地壳的。"},{"start":199.84,"end":204.08,"text":"很可能不到 300 万年前。"},{"start":204.08,"end":208.32,"text":"但它也可能就发生在末次冰期，"},{"start":208.32,"end":213.37,"text":"1.2 万到 11.5 万年前。"},{"start":213.37,"end":217.56,"text":"撞击也可能发生在冰已经覆盖格陵兰的时候，"},{"start":217.56,"end":221.78,"text":"那它会瞬间汽化数十亿吨冰，并改变"},{"start":221.78,"end":225.99,"text":"冰和水流入海洋的路线。"},{"start":225.99,"end":230.25,"text":"不管撞击发生在什么时候，当时地球上的生命都会受到深刻影响。"},{"start":230.25,"end":234.75,"text":"这么大的撞击不太可能"},{"start":234.75,"end":238.92,"text":"很快再发生，但有证据表明它可能发生在"},{"start":238.92,"end":243.0,"text":"地球历史上并不算久远的时候，这对评估今天的风险至关重要。"},{"start":243.0,"end":247.1,"text":"这是对海华沙撞击坑的第一项研究，"},{"start":247.1,"end":251.22,"text":"但它仍藏着许多等待发现的秘密。"}],"de":[],"en":[{"start":0.33,"end":4.56,"text":"In a remote area of northwest Greenland,","words":[["In","在"],["a","一个"],["remote","偏远的"],["area","地区"],["of","的"],["northwest","西北"],["Greenland,","格陵兰"]]},{"start":4.56,"end":8.75,"text":"an international team of scientists has","words":[["an","一支"],["international","国际的"],["team","团队"],["of","的"],["scientists","科学家"],["has","已"]]},{"start":8.75,"end":12.99,"text":"made a stunning discovery, buried beneath a kilometer","words":[["made","做出"],["a","一个"],["stunning","惊人的"],["discovery,","发现"],["buried","埋"],["beneath","在…下"],["a","一"],["kilometer","公里"]]},{"start":12.99,"end":17.18,"text":"of ice. It’s an impact crater …","words":[["of","的"],["ice.","冰"],["It’s","它是"],["an","一个"],["impact","撞击"],["crater","坑"],["…","…"]]},{"start":17.18,"end":21.4,"text":"300 meters deep … 31 km wide","words":[["300","300"],["meters","米"],["deep","深"],["…","…"],["31","31"],["km","公里"],["wide","宽"]]},{"start":21.4,"end":25.69,"text":"… much bigger than Washington, D.C.,","words":[["…","…"],["much","很"],["bigger","更大"],["than","比"],["Washington,","华盛顿"],["D.C.,","特区"]]},{"start":25.69,"end":29.89,"text":"even bigger than Paris, and it’s probably","words":[["even","甚至"],["bigger","更大"],["than","比"],["Paris,","巴黎"],["and","而"],["it’s","它是"],["probably","大概"]]},{"start":29.89,"end":34.15,"text":"one of the youngest large impact craters on Earth.","words":[["one","一个"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["youngest","最年轻的"],["large","大型"],["impact","撞击"],["craters","坑"],["on","在"],["Earth.","地球"]]},{"start":34.15,"end":38.48,"text":"The relentless spread of the Greenland Ice Sheet has covered the crater, obscuring","words":[["The","这"],["relentless","不断的"],["spread","扩张"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["Greenland","格陵兰"],["Ice","冰"],["Sheet","盖"],["has","已"],["covered","覆盖"],["the","这"],["crater,","坑"],["obscuring","遮蔽"]]},{"start":38.48,"end":42.7,"text":"obscuring it from view for thousands if not hundreds of thousands of years.","words":[["obscuring","遮蔽"],["it","它"],["from","从"],["view","视线"],["for","达"],["thousands","数千"],["if","若"],["not","不是"],["hundreds","数百"],["of","的"],["thousands","数千"],["of","的"],["years.","年"]]},{"start":42.7,"end":46.91,"text":"Even so, scientists say it was essentially hiding in plain sight.","words":[["Even","即便"],["so,","如此"],["scientists","科学家"],["say","说"],["it","它"],["was","曾"],["essentially","基本上"],["hiding","藏"],["in","在"],["plain","显眼"],["sight.","视线"]]},{"start":46.91,"end":51.18,"text":"So what finally revealed its presence?","words":[["So","那"],["what","什么"],["finally","最终"],["revealed","揭示"],["its","它的"],["presence?","存在"]]},{"start":51.18,"end":55.42,"text":"It all started with a rock … a map …","words":[["It","它"],["all","全"],["started","开始"],["with","以"],["a","一块"],["rock","石头"],["…","…"],["a","一张"],["map","地图"],["…","…"]]},{"start":55.42,"end":59.61,"text":"and a connection made by scientists at the Natural History Museum in Copenhagen.","words":[["and","和"],["a","一个"],["connection","联系"],["made","做出"],["by","由"],["scientists","科学家"],["at","在"],["the","这"],["Natural","自然"],["History","历史"],["Museum","博物馆"],["in","在"],["Copenhagen.","哥本哈根"]]},{"start":59.61,"end":63.92,"text":"Each day, scientists there pass by a large","words":[["Each","每"],["day,","天"],["scientists","科学家"],["there","那里"],["pass","经过"],["by","旁边"],["a","一块"],["large","巨大"]]},{"start":63.92,"end":68.12,"text":"iron meteorite found in Greenland decades ago.","words":[["iron","铁"],["meteorite","陨石"],["found","发现"],["in","在"],["Greenland","格陵兰"],["decades","几十年"],["ago.","前"]]},{"start":68.12,"end":72.33,"text":"One day, they got a new map of the bedrock topography beneath the ice sheet,","words":[["One","一"],["day,","天"],["they","他们"],["got","得到"],["a","一张"],["new","新"],["map","地图"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["bedrock","基岩"],["topography","地形"],["beneath","在…下面"],["the","这"],["ice","冰"],["sheet,","盖"]]},{"start":72.33,"end":76.55,"text":"mostly based on ice-penetrating radar data collected","words":[["mostly","主要"],["based","基于"],["on","于"],["ice-penetrating","穿冰"],["radar","雷达"],["data","数据"],["collected","收集"]]},{"start":76.55,"end":80.75,"text":"onboard NASA’s P-3 aircraft over two decades.","words":[["onboard","在…上"],["NASA’s","NASA的"],["P-3","P-3"],["aircraft","飞机"],["over","在"],["two","两"],["decades.","十年"]]},{"start":80.75,"end":84.95,"text":"This map gets more refined all the time, yet there are still areas open","words":[["This","这张"],["map","地图"],["gets","变得"],["more","更"],["refined","精细"],["all","全"],["the","这"],["time,","时候"],["yet","但"],["there","有"],["are","是"],["still","仍"],["areas","地区"],["open","开放"]]},{"start":84.95,"end":89.18,"text":"to interpretation, including the conspicuously semicircular","words":[["to","对"],["interpretation,","解读"],["including","包括"],["the","这"],["conspicuously","明显的"],["semicircular","半圆形"]]},{"start":89.18,"end":93.36,"text":"edge of the ice sheet, drained by the Hiawatha Glacier.","words":[["edge","边缘"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["ice","冰"],["sheet,","盖"],["drained","排水"],["by","由"],["the","这"],["Hiawatha","海华沙"],["Glacier.","冰川"]]},{"start":93.36,"end":97.55,"text":"There, the data showed a circular depression in the bedrock,","words":[["There,","那里"],["the","这"],["data","数据"],["showed","显示"],["a","一个"],["circular","圆形"],["depression","凹陷"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["bedrock,","基岩"]]},{"start":97.55,"end":101.77,"text":"near the region where that courtyard meteorite had been found.","words":[["near","靠近"],["the","这"],["region","地区"],["where","那里"],["that","那块"],["courtyard","院子"],["meteorite","陨石"],["had","曾"],["been","被"],["found.","发现"]]},{"start":101.77,"end":105.99,"text":"In May of 2016, the team sent the German research plane","words":[["In","在"],["May","五月"],["of","的"],["2016,","2016年"],["the","这"],["team","团队"],["sent","派"],["the","这"],["German","德国"],["research","科研"],["plane","飞机"]]},{"start":105.99,"end":110.2,"text":"Polar 6 to fly over Hiawatha Glacier with a powerful new","words":[["Polar","极地"],["6","6"],["to","去"],["fly","飞"],["over","越过"],["Hiawatha","海华沙"],["Glacier","冰川"],["with","带"],["a","一台"],["powerful","强大的"],["new","新"]]},{"start":110.2,"end":114.49,"text":"ice-penetrating radar.","words":[["ice-penetrating","穿冰"],["radar.","雷达"]]},{"start":114.49,"end":118.75,"text":"Radar waves can travel through the ice, measuring its thickness","words":[["Radar","雷达"],["waves","波"],["can","能"],["travel","穿行"],["through","穿过"],["the","这"],["ice,","冰"],["measuring","测量"],["its","它的"],["thickness","厚度"]]},{"start":118.75,"end":123.08,"text":"and internal structure. Studying data from this airborne survey,","words":[["and","和"],["internal","内部"],["structure.","结构"],["Studying","研究"],["data","数据"],["from","来自"],["this","这个"],["airborne","航空"],["survey,","测量"]]},{"start":123.08,"end":127.34,"text":"the scientists confirmed the telltale bowl shape and central peaks","words":[["the","这"],["scientists","科学家"],["confirmed","确认"],["the","这"],["telltale","明显的"],["bowl","碗"],["shape","形状"],["and","和"],["central","中央"],["peaks","峰"]]},{"start":127.34,"end":131.59,"text":"beneath Hiawatha Glacier. They also found that the oldest ice","words":[["beneath","在…下面"],["Hiawatha","海华沙"],["Glacier.","冰川"],["They","他们"],["also","也"],["found","发现"],["that","那"],["the","这"],["oldest","最古老的"],["ice","冰"]]},{"start":131.59,"end":135.82,"text":"in this crater was actually fairly young, by Greenland standards,","words":[["in","在"],["this","这个"],["crater","坑"],["was","曾"],["actually","其实"],["fairly","相当"],["young,","年轻"],["by","按"],["Greenland","格陵兰"],["standards,","标准"]]},{"start":135.82,"end":139.93,"text":"and had experienced a great disturbance in its flow toward the end","words":[["and","和"],["had","曾"],["experienced","经历"],["a","一次"],["great","巨大的"],["disturbance","扰动"],["in","在"],["its","它的"],["flow","流动"],["toward","向"],["the","这"],["end","末尾"]]},{"start":139.93,"end":144.23,"text":"of the last ice age.","words":[["of","的"],["the","这"],["last","末次"],["ice","冰"],["age.","期"]]},{"start":144.23,"end":148.47,"text":"The team then visited the area on foot, and in sediments deposited by a river","words":[["The","这"],["team","团队"],["then","然后"],["visited","去了"],["the","这"],["area","地区"],["on","用"],["foot,","脚"],["and","和"],["in","在"],["sediments","沉积物"],["deposited","沉积"],["by","由"],["a","一条"],["river","河"]]},{"start":148.47,"end":152.69,"text":"draining out of the glacier, they found grains of the mineral quartz that showed signs","words":[["draining","流"],["out","出"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["glacier,","冰川"],["they","他们"],["found","发现"],["grains","颗粒"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["mineral","矿物"],["quartz","石英"],["that","那"],["showed","显示"],["signs","迹象"]]},{"start":152.69,"end":156.95,"text":"of being physically shocked in a massive impact.","words":[["of","的"],["being","被"],["physically","物理地"],["shocked","冲击"],["in","在"],["a","一次"],["massive","巨大的"],["impact.","撞击"]]},{"start":156.95,"end":161.13,"text":"Models suggest, the asteroid was more than a kilometer wide.","words":[["Models","模型"],["suggest,","表明"],["the","这"],["asteroid","小行星"],["was","曾"],["more","超过"],["than","于"],["a","一"],["kilometer","公里"],["wide.","宽"]]},{"start":161.13,"end":165.32,"text":"The Hiawatha crater is one of the 25 largest known","words":[["The","这"],["Hiawatha","海华沙"],["crater","坑"],["is","是"],["one","一个"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["25","25"],["largest","最大"],["known","已知"]]},{"start":165.32,"end":169.95,"text":"impact craters on Earth, and the first found under any of","words":[["impact","撞击"],["craters","坑"],["on","在"],["Earth,","地球"],["and","和"],["the","这"],["first","第一个"],["found","发现"],["under","在…下"],["any","任何"],["of","的"]]},{"start":169.95,"end":174.26,"text":"our planet’s ice sheets.Crucially, the Hiawatha impact","words":[["our","我们的"],["planet’s","行星的"],["ice","冰"],["sheets.Crucially,","盖。关键是，"],["the","这"],["Hiawatha","海华沙"],["impact","撞击"]]},{"start":174.26,"end":178.55,"text":"crater still looks like an impact crater, even though it’s covered by ice","words":[["crater","坑"],["still","仍"],["looks","看起来"],["like","像"],["an","一个"],["impact","撞击"],["crater,","坑"],["even","即使"],["though","尽管"],["it’s","它是"],["covered","覆盖"],["by","被"],["ice","冰"]]},{"start":178.55,"end":182.75,"text":"and seems to be rapidly eroding. The data as a whole","words":[["and","和"],["seems","似乎"],["to","去"],["be","是"],["rapidly","快速"],["eroding.","侵蚀"],["The","这"],["data","数据"],["as","作为"],["a","一个"],["whole","整体"]]},{"start":182.75,"end":187.03,"text":"suggests it’s quite young – geologically speaking","words":[["suggests","表明"],["it’s","它是"],["quite","相当"],["young","年轻"],["–","–"],["geologically","地质上"],["speaking","说"]]},{"start":187.03,"end":191.32,"text":"But we don’t know exactly when an asteroid sped","words":[["But","但"],["we","我们"],["don’t","不"],["know","知道"],["exactly","确切"],["when","何时"],["an","一颗"],["asteroid","小行星"],["sped","冲"]]},{"start":191.32,"end":195.55,"text":"toward Earth, through the atmosphere, and into the","words":[["toward","向"],["Earth,","地球"],["through","穿过"],["the","这"],["atmosphere,","大气层"],["and","和"],["into","进"],["the","这"]]},{"start":195.55,"end":199.84,"text":"planet’s crust in Northwest Greenland.","words":[["planet’s","行星的"],["crust","地壳"],["in","在"],["Northwest","西北"],["Greenland.","格陵兰"]]},{"start":199.84,"end":204.08,"text":"It was likely less than 3 million years ago.","words":[["It","它"],["was","曾"],["likely","很可能"],["less","少"],["than","于"],["3","3"],["million","百万"],["years","年"],["ago.","前"]]},{"start":204.08,"end":208.32,"text":"But it might have been as recently as during the last ice age,","words":[["But","但"],["it","它"],["might","可能"],["have","有"],["been","是"],["as","一样"],["recently","晚近"],["as","一样"],["during","在…期间"],["the","这"],["last","末次"],["ice","冰"],["age,","期"]]},{"start":208.32,"end":213.37,"text":"12 to 115 thousand years ago.","words":[["12","12"],["to","到"],["115","115"],["thousand","千"],["years","年"],["ago.","前"]]},{"start":213.37,"end":217.56,"text":"The impact could have also occurred when ice already covered Greenland","words":[["The","这"],["impact","撞击"],["could","可能"],["have","有"],["also","也"],["occurred","发生"],["when","当"],["ice","冰"],["already","已经"],["covered","覆盖"],["Greenland","格陵兰"]]},{"start":217.56,"end":221.78,"text":"and it would have instantly vaporized billions of tons of ice and re-routed","words":[["and","而"],["it","它"],["would","会"],["have","有"],["instantly","瞬间"],["vaporized","汽化"],["billions","数十亿"],["of","的"],["tons","吨"],["of","的"],["ice","冰"],["and","和"],["re-routed","改道"]]},{"start":221.78,"end":225.99,"text":"the flow of ice and water into the ocean.","words":[["the","这"],["flow","流动"],["of","的"],["ice","冰"],["and","和"],["water","水"],["into","进"],["the","这"],["ocean.","海洋"]]},{"start":225.99,"end":230.25,"text":"Whenever the impact happened, life on Earth at the time would have been profoundly affected.","words":[["Whenever","无论何时"],["the","这"],["impact","撞击"],["happened,","发生"],["life","生命"],["on","在"],["Earth","地球"],["at","在"],["the","这"],["time","时候"],["would","会"],["have","有"],["been","被"],["profoundly","深刻地"],["affected.","影响"]]},{"start":230.25,"end":234.75,"text":"An impact of this size is unlikely","words":[["An","一次"],["impact","撞击"],["of","的"],["this","这个"],["size","大小"],["is","是"],["unlikely","不太可能"]]},{"start":234.75,"end":238.92,"text":"to happen again soon, but evidence that it might have happened","words":[["to","去"],["happen","发生"],["again","再"],["soon,","很快"],["but","但"],["evidence","证据"],["that","那"],["it","它"],["might","可能"],["have","有"],["happened","发生"]]},{"start":238.92,"end":243.0,"text":"not so long ago, in Earth’s history is essential to assessing the risk today.","words":[["not","不"],["so","那么"],["long","久"],["ago,","前"],["in","在"],["Earth’s","地球的"],["history","历史"],["is","是"],["essential","至关重要"],["to","对"],["assessing","评估"],["the","这"],["risk","风险"],["today.","今天"]]},{"start":243.0,"end":247.1,"text":"This is the first study of the Hiawatha","words":[["This","这"],["is","是"],["the","这"],["first","第一项"],["study","研究"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["Hiawatha","海华沙"]]},{"start":247.1,"end":251.22,"text":"impact crater, but it still holds many secrets waiting to be discovered.","words":[["impact","撞击"],["crater,","坑"],["but","但"],["it","它"],["still","仍"],["holds","藏着"],["many","许多"],["secrets","秘密"],["waiting","等待"],["to","去"],["be","被"],["discovered.","发现"]]}]}